<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan domestic vehicle sales up 14.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan domestic vehicle sales up 14.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle sales rose 14.9 percent in January from a year earlier to 336,642 units, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association (JADA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>It was the fifth straight month in which domestic sales rose on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The January sales breakdown was as follows (with percentage</p>
<p>changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		234,621  up   20.0 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc    56,288  up   18.0 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  178,333  up   20.7 percent</p>
<p> Trucks		    101,261  up    4.6 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	    9,307  up   15.4 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	   91,954  up    3.6 percent</p>
<p> Buses			   760  up    1.7 percent</p>
<p>January sales included 24,177 imported vehicles, up 4.1 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>January vehicle sales by five major Japanese makers were as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     126,008  up   17.4 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	69,870  up    2.7 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 38,373  up   54.5 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 28,509  up    4.7 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 23,775  up   22.7 percent</p>
</text>
